# Part VIII — What the Existing Data Say About the Proposed Mechanism

### [DIRECTLY FROM DATA]

The following claims are **false without additional hypotheses**:

$$
\boxed{\text{Every persistent obstruction can be pushed away from branching vertices.}}
$$

and

$$
\boxed{\text{Every persistence layer automatically costs two degree-2 vertices.}}
$$

The 6-vertex double star disproves both unrestricted ideas.

### [DIRECTLY FROM DATA]

The existing \(n\le19\) computation does not contain a genuine actual-\(q\) obstruction.

Therefore it cannot confirm or refute the restricted versions that would be needed for the target theorem.

### [STRUCTURAL HYPOTHESIS]

The most plausible repair is therefore:

$$
\boxed{
\text{first isolate a minimal actual-}q\text{ counterexample,}
}
$$

then prove that its critical obstruction can be represented by **disjoint critical threads**.

This is materially stronger than saying "branching is harmless."

